== Reward ==

* [[Chapter V, Ashes in the Margins]]
* [[Holiday Gift]]*

== Walkthrough ==

You say, 'Hail, Isolde Winterveil'
: Isolde Winterveil says, 'The Icestar remembers much — but it is not whole. And so, some names fade. There is one… a good soul, long unthanked. His name is gone from my memory, but I've felt the echo. [Take this shard] of memory. It may stir something in someone who once knew him.'

You say, 'I will take this shard.'
: Isolde Winterveil says, 'Thank you, Norrathian. Please [find] the one whose name is forgotten.'
You say, 'Find who?'
: Isolde Winterveil says, 'I remember snow. Mountains... no — hills. A patrol along an old road. He served without praise, yet never faltered. There is a guard in the hills that surround Qeynos. I think his name began with an L? Lamet? Lamile? Something like that. Do you see how memory decays without the Icestar's light? Making it whole again is no longer a wish — it's a necessity. Before more names are lost. Bring me back anything that can help restore this memory.'

You receive [[Frosted Memory Shard]]

You say, 'Hail, [[Guard Lammel]]'
: Guard Lammel says, 'I've wandered these hills for many years. Seen many things.'
: Guard Lammel says, '...That mark... I haven't seen it in years. There was a fellow. Younger. Always volunteered for the winter watch. Shared his cloak with a merchant once. Dug out a buried traveler near Blackburrow without orders. No one ever remembered his name. Not even me. While the name escapes me, the memory does not. He [mattered].'

You say, 'Who mattered?'

: Guard Lammel says, 'Thank you. Yes, If someone out there still holds a memory of him, he mattered for sure. The memory of him warms my heart once again. Here, take this broach - it was his. I’ve held onto it in my backpack for years now in case I ever ran into him again. Maybe you can find him now.'

Give [[Guard Lammel]] the [[Frosted Memory Shard]].

You receive a [[Frosted Broach]]. Return to Eastern Waste and turn in a [[Frosted Broach]] to Isolde Winterveil.

Upon turning in Frosted Broach to Isolde Winterviel, 

: Isolde Winterveil places the broach on a frozen tablet. It dissolves into silver light, etching new text onto a frosted page. She says, 'Then the echo has found its voice. Another soul no longer lost. The margins of the preamble grow fuller. And the Icestar shines a little brighter.'

You receive [[Chapter V, Ashes in the Margins]] and a [[Holiday Gift]]*.


'''* NOTE: You will only receive the Holiday Gift from this quest the first time you complete it. Due to abuse of the questline, repeatable attempts had the Holiday Gift removed.'''

